ned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}+1$, find $f(A).$\n\n| $f(A)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+1 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279493/field-1" "q-279493/field-2" "q-279493/field-3" "q-279493/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279493"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279495/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "d1d8b520-e231-5243-9511-01de95332e98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279495/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "ddaa81b6-67eb-521a-b24c-0eeca1554dba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279495/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "92c7d2eb-fbf8-5aaa-9a94-8d8dff49661e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.