field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279495/field-4/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-279495/field-4/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279495" :question/id #uuid "837dfeab-e27d-5728-9d16-79567dd4af9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279495" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $H=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}+3X+2$, find $f(H).$\n\n| $f(H)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(H)={H}^{2}+3H+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${H}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{2} & =H\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(H):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(H) & ={H}^{2}+3H+2I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7+9+2 & -3+(-3)+0 \\\\ 6+6+0 & -2+0+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 & -6 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279495/field-1" "q-279495/field-2" "q-279495/field-3" "q-279495/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279495"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-78348"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find $f(C)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-2X-5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-2X-5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-2X-5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(C)={C}^{2}-2C-5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(C):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(C) & ={C}^{2}-2C-5I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7-2-5 & 4-4-0 \\\\ 6-6-0 & 7-2-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4414"] :question/problem "Find $A^4$ given that $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find $A^2,$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}81 & 0 \\\\ 100 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4417"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate $D^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & =-{D}^{2}+3D+2I \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3+2 & 10+15+0 \\\\ 0 & -9-9+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 25 \\\\ 0 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
